  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In first step, acetylation of aniline&nbsp;occurs. This process is done to lower the activating nature of amine otherwise poly substitution will occur.</p><p>On bromination, bromine group is directed at para position. In ortho&nbsp;position repulsion will dominate due to which its percentage of ortho product is less.&nbsp; <img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/55b5f149-1249-48f0-a57c-d958ba2114da-image.png\" style=\"width: 901px; height: 231px;\" /></p>",
